# npm
#
# The lockfile is versioned, deliberately. Ignoring it is right for a library
# that others install; for an application it means no two installs are
# guaranteed alike, no build is reproducible, and `npm ci` — which is what CI
# needs — cannot run at all. The API repository already versioned its own.
yarn.lock

# Build output
/build
/dist

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.swp

# Le banc d'essai a ses propres dépendances.
verif/node_modules
